format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATANO, TAKAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAMOTO, AKIHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI, HIROKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Optical parts each having a positive thermal expansion coefficient are disposed in inner holes formed in specified locations on a base material having a negative thermal expansion coefficient of -10 to -120 x 10&lt;-7&gt;/ DEG C within a temp. range of -40 to 100  DEG C. In addition, a plurality of specified locations spaced apart from each other in a hole axial direction of each of inner holes in optical parts are fixed to the base material.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des parties optiques, chacune ayant un coefficient de dilatation thermique positif, disposées dans des trous intérieurs formés à des emplacements définis sur une matière de base dont le coefficient de dilatation thermique négatif est de -10 à -120 X 10&lt;-7&gt;/ DEG C dans une plage de températures allant de -40 à 100  DEG C. Par ailleurs, une pluralité d'emplacements spécifiques espacés les uns des autres et disposés dans un sens axial par rapport aux trous intérieurs ménagés dans les parties optiques sont fixés à la matière de base.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-docum